(text "Source: https://nicekeyboards.com/docs/nice-nano/pinout-schematic (pinout-v2.png, fetched 2026-11-05).\nPin names and D numbers are copied from that image (Dn = Arduino label). Pin numbers 1-26 are ours.\nBATTERY+ appears twice on the front, as on the image. When P0.13 is set low, power to 3.3V is cut off.\nBack pads (SWC, SWD, P1.01, P1.02, P1.07, BOOST) are named as on the image; their positions here are approximate.\nBOOST: bridging the back jumper raises the charge rate from 100 mA to 500 mA (only for batteries > 500 mAh)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 142.960 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "94ac5cb3-8f5f-564b-82af-ab7b391040af"))
